From: CarPlay C0 lane (2026-11-22)
Subject: 0519 sweet_nub: construct the abstract controller instance ourselves

The 0518 boot answered why S2 never passed: the explicit kext load works (three load -> 0x0
lines, metaclass 0xfffffff006a9a708 found) but mc->alloc() returns NULL while getClassSize()
reports 504. That is the IOKit abstract-class shape (OSDefineMetaClassAndAbstractStructors):
MetaClass::alloc() is the base "return NULL", and the 18 __cxa_pure_virtual slots we censused
are the same fact. The registry can therefore never hand us an IOUSBDeviceController.

0519 prints control allocations (IOService, IOUSBDeviceConfigurator, IOUSBDeviceInterface,
AppleSynopsysOTGDevice, AppleVirtIOUSBDeviceController) and then builds the instance the way
alloc would have: OSObject::operator new (zeroed kheap memory) + install the class's published
vtable + one retain. init() stays where it already is in the probe flow, after the vtable copy
is patched, so a failure there is reported and skipped instead of patching a live object.

Found on the device, not from a guess: 0518 S02 printed "alloc -> 0, classSize 504" at 10.194 s.

--- a/libkern/c++/sweet_nub.cpp
+++ b/libkern/c++/sweet_nub.cpp
@@ -181,6 +181,56 @@
 	IOService *ctl = (IOService *)mc->alloc();
 	printf("SWEET NUB: alloc -> %p, classSize %u, own class %s\n", ctl, mc->getClassSize(),
 	    ctl != NULL ? ctl->getMetaClass()->getClassName() : "-");
+	if (ctl == NULL) {
+		/*
+		 * 0519: on the 0518 boot this line was `alloc -> 0, classSize 504`. A registered class
+		 * whose alloc returns NULL while reporting a plausible instance size is the IOKit
+		 * abstract-class shape: OSDefineMetaClassAndAbstractStructors defines MetaClass::alloc()
+		 * as the base "return NULL" (OSObject::MetaClass::alloc), and the 18 __cxa_pure_virtual
+		 * vtable slots we censused are the other half of the same fact. So the base cannot be
+		 * allocated through the registry at all; the probe has to build the instance itself,
+		 * which is what it was always going to patch anyway.
+		 *
+		 * First print the control allocations: IOService must succeed, the two shipped concrete
+		 * subclasses say which provider classes this build actually has. Then construct the
+		 * base the way alloc would have: operator new (zeroed, kheap) + install the class's
+		 * published vtable + one retain for the probe's own owner count. init() stays where it
+		 * is in the normal flow (after the vtable copy is patched).
+		 */
+		static const char *probe_classes[] = {
+			"IOService",
+			"IOUSBDeviceController",
+			"IOUSBDeviceConfigurator",
+			"IOUSBDeviceInterface",
+			"AppleSynopsysOTGDevice",
+			"AppleVirtIOUSBDeviceController",
+		};
+		for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof(probe_classes) / sizeof(probe_classes[0]); i++) {
+			const OSSymbol *sym = OSSymbol::withCStringNoCopy(probe_classes[i]);
+			const OSMetaClass *m = sym != NULL ? OSMetaClass::getMetaClassWithName(sym) : NULL;
+			OSObject *o = m != NULL ? m->alloc() : NULL;
+			printf("SWEET NUB: probe-alloc %s: meta %p size %u -> %p%s%s\n",
+			    probe_classes[i], m, m != NULL ? m->getClassSize() : 0, o,
+			    o != NULL ? " class " : "",
+			    o != NULL ? o->getMetaClass()->getClassName() : "");
+			if (o != NULL) {
+				o->release();
+			}
+		}
+		{
+			size_t size = (size_t)mc->getClassSize();
+			void *mem = OSObject::operator new(size);
+			printf("SWEET NUB: manual construction of %s: %u bytes at %p\n", SWEET_NUB_CLASS,
+			    (unsigned)size, mem);
+			if (mem != NULL) {
+				*(void ***)mem = (void **)SWEET_NUB_CTL_VTABLE;
+				ctl = (IOService *)mem;
+				ctl->retain();
+				printf("SWEET NUB: manual -> %p, own class %s\n", ctl,
+				    ctl->getMetaClass()->getClassName());
+			}
+		}
+	}
 	if (ctl == NULL) {
 		return;
 	}
